      "math_academy_id": "q-125516",
      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "Find the median of the random variable $X$ if the cumulative distribution function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0, \\\\ \\frac{x}{3}, & 0\\le x\\le 2 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{4}}{195}+\\frac{38}{65}, & 2<x\\le 3, \\\\ 1, & x>3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The median of a random variable $X$ is the number $m$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le m)=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nSince $F(2)=\\frac{2}{3}>\\frac{1}{2},$ we have $0\\le m\\le 2.$\n\nTherefore, the median is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{m}{3}=\\frac{1}{2}\\,⇒\\,m=\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$",
